{
 "_comment": "Hand-authored by this project (our own content, no disc tables copied). Extra rewards that can come on top of a fishing win. The disc catch (a battle: slot 4 Cardmon, slot 7 water Digimon) is never touched. Item ids are the game's own item numbers; names are checked by tests/fishing-extras.test.js. BALANCE RULE: see \"balance\".",
 "balance": {
  "rule": "Per catch the extra chance is 3 to 8 percent in total. Tier = the stage's slot-4 Cardmon level (12, 27, 42, 47 -> tier 1..4), which is how far the story has got when that stage's water is fished. An item's worth is its shop buy price (or twice its sell price when the shop never sells it). A normal entry is worth no more than the tier ceiling, which is about what the shops already sell at that point; a very rare entry (1 percent or less) may be worth up to double the ceiling. Bits never exceed the smallest bits one win of that tier's big water Digimon pays. Card packs are the same item class the disc's own Cardmon catch pays on the same cast. The extra is paid only when the fight is won, never when the Digimon flees.",
  "item_value_ceiling": {
   "1": 130,
   "2": 550,
   "3": 1300,
   "4": 2500
  },
  "very_rare_multiplier": 2,
  "very_rare_max_percent": 1,
  "bits_ceiling": {
   "1": 60,
   "2": 100,
   "3": 150,
   "4": 400
  },
  "min_total_percent": 3,
  "max_total_percent": 8,
  "tier_by_cardmon_level": {
   "12": 1,
   "27": 2,
   "42": 3,
   "47": 4
  },
  "card_pack_item_ids": [
   375,
   377,
   380,
   390
  ]
 },
 "hints": [
  "A visit to the water gives you sixteen casts. Leave the map and come back for sixteen more.",
  "One band of the meter hooks a Cardmon. The other band hooks the big Digimon of these waters.",
  "No pole, no cast. The fishing spots only open once you own the fishing pole.",
  "Kick the trees near the water too. Only one tree on each map holds a Digimon."
 ],
